From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadim Bauer <vb@container-registry.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:30:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(registry/storage/driver/s3-aws): add spooldir to
 buffer upload parts on disk

The S3 driver buffers one chunksize-sized part per in-flight blob
upload in memory, so registry memory grows linearly with the number of
concurrent pushes (about 2x chunksize each, roughly 20MiB per upload at
the default 10MiB chunk size). Under concurrent push load this is a
common cause of registry OOM kills; the only existing knob is lowering
chunksize, which trades memory for more API calls.

Add an optional spooldir parameter. When set, pending part data is
written to a temporary file per upload and streamed to S3 from disk via
a SectionReader, bounding per-upload heap usage at O(copy buffer)
regardless of concurrency. When unset, behaviour is unchanged.

Measured with 32 concurrent 100MB blob uploads at the default 10MiB
chunk size: peak heap drops from 724MiB to 15MiB with no throughput
change, and uploaded content verified byte-identical.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Bauer <vb@container-registry.com>
Upstream: https://github.com/distribution/distribution/pull/4920
